Package: Pando
Version: 2.0.11
Type: Package
Title: Inferring regulomes from multi-modal single-cell genomics data
Authors@R: person(given = "Jonas Simon",
               family = "Fleck",
               role = c("aut", "cre"),
               email = "jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch",
               comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4686-7254"))
Maintainer: Jonas Simon Fleck <jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch>
Description: Pando jointly uses scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq measurements to infer
    regulatory relationships between TF-binding site pairs and target genes.
    For two or more conditions within a broad cell type, infer_condition_grn
    retains the original Pando regulatory-domain, motif, peak-target-correlation
    and TF-target-correlation candidate logic while producing directly
    comparable condition coefficients. Candidate discovery is run on all
    eligible-condition cells pooled together and independently within each
    condition. Exact target-TF-region triples passing both configured correlation
    gates in the pooled/global calculation or in at least one condition are
    deduplicated into one frozen common dictionary. Every condition uses this
    identical ordered dictionary, the original TF-by-ATAC interaction predictor,
    an equal-condition within-condition RMS predictor scale, condition-specific
    intercepts and one pooled Gaussian residual scale. Conditional coefficients
    are estimated jointly by E-star with the fixed production deviation threshold
    z=0.25. The Q-orthogonal shared component is the unpenalized joint MLE; only
    identifiable condition-deviation coordinates receive the information-scaled
    sparse penalty. A predeclared reference ordering is preferred for the
    identifiable contrast tree, with non-reference identifiable contrasts used
    when the reference coordinate is not identifiable. Zero-information
    contrasts are fixed to sharing as a boundary convention and are marked
    separately from penalty-selected fusion. Exact-zero deviations define fusion
    components. After that structure is frozen, a reduced joint model with
    condition-specific intercepts provides full correlated joint covariance,
    inference estimates, standard errors and Wald P values. P values are BH
    adjusted within each condition-by-target family. The production effect always
    remains the continuous E-star coefficient. An exact edge is handed to
    RegCompass only when every condition has a valid production coefficient and
    at least one condition has BH-adjusted P < 0.05; once admitted, the edge is
    retained in every condition with its own continuous production coefficient.
    Full-data target R-squared remains diagnostic and is not a conditional-GRN
    topology gate. Standard infer_grn retains its independent Gaussian GLM and
    single-task ridge implementations. Target-parallel candidate discovery and
    fitting use target-specific payload batches, and independent cell-type jobs
    can be dispatched through BiocParallel.
